Description: Fix CVE-2026-42037 - HTTP header injection via CRLF in multipart Content-Type
 The FormDataPart constructor in lib/helpers/formDataToStream.js embedded
 the user-controlled value.type directly into the Content-Type header
 without sanitizing CR/LF characters. A crafted Blob/File-like value with
 a type containing "\r\n" could inject additional MIME headers or split
 the multipart part, enabling header injection in outgoing requests.
 .
 The fix coerces value.type to a string and strips all CR and LF
 characters before interpolating it into the Content-Type header.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/2271ea2cfb66fea29ab0e9659dd2cd56e984f7b3
Author: Jason Saayman <jasonsaayman@gmail.com>
CVE: CVE-2026-42037
Last-Update: 2026-05-30

